{
  "associatedLayout": "Level Editor",
  "name": "SaveCodeLE",
  "events": [
    {
      "type": "BuiltinCommonInstructions::Comment",
      "color": {
        "b": 109,
        "g": 230,
        "r": 255,
        "textB": 0,
        "textG": 0,
        "textR": 0
      },
      "comment": "These events are responsible for creating the save code.\n\nIf you've introduced a new variable in trackconf or any other block and want it to be saved, you need to add a new event within the \"Save block's object variables\" group.\n\nThe event condition should verify the block name for which you want to save the variables. The action of the event should append a new string to the scene variable SaveCode. The string should follow this format:\n\nBlocks.ObjectName()+\":\"+ToString(Blocks.X())+\",\"+ToString(Blocks.Y())+\",\"+ToString(Blocks.Angle())+\":\"+<BLOCK NAME>.<OBJECT VARIABLE NAME>+\"/\"\n\n\nTo add more object variables simply add the below line before the (\"/\"): \n\n\":\"+<BLOCK NAME>.<OBJECT VARIABLE NAME>+\n\n\nLike this:\nBlocks.ObjectName()+\":\"+ToString(Blocks.X())+\",\"+ToString(Blocks.Y())+\",\"+ToString(Blocks.Angle())+\":\"+<BLOCK NAME>.<OBJECT VARIABLE NAME>+\":\"+<BLOCK NAME>.<OBJECT VARIABLE NAME 2>+\"/\"\n\n\nRemember to update the LoadSave function to account for your variables and ensure they are loaded\n!"
    },
    {
      "type": "BuiltinCommonInstructions::Standard",
      "conditions": [],
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": {
            "value": "ModVarSceneTxt"
          },
          "parameters": [
            "SaveCode",
            "=",
            "\"\""
          ]
        }
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "type": "BuiltinCommonInstructions::ForEach",
          "object": "Blocks",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "type": {
                "value": "Layer"
              },
              "parameters": [
